    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d546">

                <pb facs="0752" n="664" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg664"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 840.48/1</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the United States</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Reading</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Food
                        Administrator</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hoover</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-13">13 <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >December</hi>, 1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Hoover</hi>: As soon as you have had time
                    to consider the document I sent to you through the good offices of M.
                        Clementel,<anchor n="30" xml:id="d546-f1"/> I should like to know whether
                    you accept its terms or in what respects you disagree with it.</p>
                <p>After you left we devoted ourselves to putting the result of our deliberations
                    into formal shape and trust that the outcome will meet with your approval. Of
                    course I bear in mind that when you left no document had been prepared and that
                    in so far as you expressed assent it was in a conversation which was not as
                    precise as in a document.</p>
                <p>Until I hear from you I fear no progress can be made.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reading</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d546-f1" n="30" xml:id="d546-f1-content">
                <p>See the report of the committee appointed by the Allied Premiers to consider
                    victualling and supply of allied, neutral, and enemy countries, <ref
                        target="#pg654">p. 654</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
